{
  "_about": [
    "Part 28 « Envoyer les heures aux clients »: THE table of « what a client must be told now » (REARRANGE.md §1.3, §3.1-§3.2, §3.5).",
    "Read by BOTH twins: src/domain/jobs/told.test.ts (tellNow / tellState / tellKind of src/domain/jobs/told.ts) and tests/db/textos-journee.test.mjs T1 (public.tell_now / public.tell_state). The same case must give the same answer in both.",
    "job: defaults.job, then the case's job over it (a shallow merge, like jsonb ||). Every key is a column of public.jobs as it is, EXCEPT day and told_day: they are DAYS FROM TODAY (0 = today = public.local_today() on the database, ctx.today in the app; 3 = in three days; -1 = yesterday; null stays null). SQL: replace the two numbers by local_today() + n, then jsonb_populate_record(null::public.jobs, job).",
    "settings: defaults.settings, then the case's settings over it = the keys of settings.booking for that case (windows_on and roads_on are what windows_on() / roads_on() must answer). rewin ABSENT = the key is not in booking; rewin PRESENT = that JSON value written as it is (a JSON null included).",
    "now_min: public.now_min() pinned (defaults.now_min unless the case gives one); it only matters for a job of today.",
    "want.now = tell_now(j) with day as days from today; rewin and drift are booleans (a SQL null would read as false: no case here gives one). want.state = tell_state(j): 'new' | 'changed' | 'drift' | 'ok' | null. want.kind = the text a due job gets: 'booking' (never told), 'window' (told « dans la journée », now a window on the same day), 'moved' (any other change); null when not due ('drift', 'ok', null).",
    "customer, messages_on and want.list (some cases only) are for tell_list (phone_ok, sms_ok, kind_on): tell_state looks at neither the phone nor Réglages → Textos (such a client stays due until « Je l'ai averti »). Default customer: phone '5145550101', sms_ok true; default messages_on: {}.",
    "lists: one world of several appointments for dueOn / driftOn / clientsDue / dueDays (the app) and tell_list (the server): id and customer are labels (give each its own uuid; customer null = an appointment with no customer). lists.days[D].due = the due appointments listed on day D (day = D or told_day = D), in tell_list's order (now.day, now.start nulls first, number); drift = that day's « en retard sur sa plage » rows; n = distinct clients (an appointment with no customer counts as one). lists.dueDays = every day from today with n > 0, in date order; total = distinct clients over all of them.",
    "Timestamps are compared as instants to the microsecond (two cases sit in the same millisecond)."
  ],
